From ecd5b6494a5343e363826987a5b08c670dfce463 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:55:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): a pinned route's quota wall shows its reset and
 Choose a model, not "internal problem"

A chat explicitly pinned to a walled subscription route (openai-codex/gpt-6-astra, quota out until a
known reset) is refused before the turn with failure_reason route_refused and the backend's own
sentence (agent.model_routing_walls.held_reply: the reset in PT, /model). The descriptor was a bare
{layer: gateway, code: route_refused}, so Desktop drew the gateway layer's generic "Hermes hit an
internal problem ... Send your message again" card, and the transcript kept "Your request was not
processed. Send it again ...", advice that cannot work until the reset and never names the fix.

Backend:
- agent/error_surface.py: a route_refused descriptor carries the turn's final_response as `message`.
- gateway/run_turn_runner.py: `_resolution_failure_result` stamps the route refusal's error_surface
  and a refusal_notice on the result (like session_policy.refused_turn_result), so the live
  message.complete carries the card and settlement commits it on the failed-turn boundary
  (display_metadata) for a reopened chat.
- gateway_refusal_boundary writes `refusal_notice` as the boundary copy when present; the messaging
  path's failed-turn notice for route_refused is the same ROUTE_REFUSED_TURN_NOTICE ("Your request
  was not processed."), with no "Send it again".

Desktop:
- route_refused is an error code with its own title/fallback body in every locale; its body is the
  backend sentence (`message`), and its one action is Choose a model (no Retry).
- turnFailure: an older backend's route_refused frame without `message` uses the turn text (minus
  an appended failed-turn notice) as the body.

Tests: RED on the source-only revert, GREEN after: route-refused-completion.test.tsx (live frame,
with and without `message`; generic gateway control), assistant-message.test.tsx (rendered card:
sentence, title, Choose a model, no Retry; host_error control keeps the generic card),
chat-messages.test.ts (reopened boundary row), tests/gateway/test_route_refused_card.py.
session_busy / content-policy / terminal-error suites unchanged and green.
